Let an element's tooltip builder show nothing

An element whose tooltip has something to say only some of the time has
to leave its tooltip builder off while it has nothing to say, and an
element rendered without a builder forgets the state of its tooltip,
including a tooltip a press put away, which then comes back at the next
nudge of the pointer. Add optional_tooltip, whose builder may return no
view, as InteractiveText's does, and refresh the window after building
a tooltip only where one was built or a shown one was taken down.

